{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance Annual General Adjustment 5% cap (Measure BB)","requirement":"The Annual General Adjustment for fully covered units is capped at a maximum of 5%, even if the Rent Ordinance formula yields more; banked unused AGAs may still be applied. Landlords may petition for increases only for completed capital improvements.","key_value":"5% maximum annual general adjustment","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units include most multifamily properties built before 1980 and single-family homes with tenancies begun before 1996. Government-owned or -subsidized units are now fully or partially covered; post-1980 new construction, most single-family homes and condominiums are partially covered.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"covered","op":"before","date":"1980","basis":"construction"},{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1980","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"},{"type":"other","text":"Government-owned or -subsidized units are now fully or partially covered depending on unit type and federal or state law."}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Most units in multifamily properties built before 1980","New Construction Units (units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980)","Government-owned or -subsidized rental units like Section 8 and Shelter + Care units are Now Fully or Partially Covered by the Rent Ordinance"]},"exemptions":"Units where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with a landlord who did not live on the property at the start of the tenancy; units where federal law, state law or administrative regulation prohibits rent control (e.g. Section 202, Section 811, certain HUD-mortgaged projects) are only partially covered.","penalty":"The Rent Board may adopt fines for noncompliance with the Ordinance's registration requirements, including failure to timely report tenancy information.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Units are fully or partially covered depending on whether federal law, state law or administrative regulation exempts the unit from the rent control provisions.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance just cause eviction requirements (Measure BB)","requirement":"Tenants in covered units may be evicted only for just cause. Nonpayment eviction requires debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent, eviction for refusing to sign a substantially similar lease is barred, and lease-breach eviction needs substantial actual harm.","key_value":"1 month's Fair Market Rent (nonpayment threshold)","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
